<!--
The ONE structMap the judge walks, spelt out in XPath 1.0 so that rules scoped to it cannot
accidentally judge an unchosen sibling map (which is preserved as parsed and never edited).
The native code makes the same choice the platform's parser makes (CONTRACT.md, "Physical
structMap selection") and refuses a document whose choice would fall on a map typed neither
physical nor at all - so by the time these rules run, the chosen map is one of these two:

  chosenExplicit - the first structMap whose TYPE is "physical" in any ASCII case;
  chosenUntyped  - otherwise, the first structMap with no TYPE.

Shared by common.sch, platform-tier.sch and eprints-tier.sch, which pull it in as an external
parameter entity. Only tools/compile_schematron.py reads the .sch sources; the compiled XSLT
has these expansions written out.
-->
<!ENTITY physicalType "translate(@TYPE, 'PHYSICAL', 'physical') = 'physical'">
<!ENTITY chosenExplicit "mets:structMap[&physicalType;][not(preceding-sibling::mets:structMap[&physicalType;])]">
<!ENTITY chosenUntyped "mets:structMap[not(@TYPE)][not(preceding-sibling::mets:structMap[not(@TYPE)])][not(../mets:structMap[&physicalType;])]">
